// The RSA-OAEP encryption negative-composition probe world: the minimal
// consumer of `rsa-oaep-encrypt`, which the in-guest provider deliberately
// does not export (encryption runs secret plaintext through
// non-constant-time bignum arithmetic — see rust/guest-provider/README.md).
// The class-D gate (`just conformance-ct::class-d`) builds a dummy component
// of this world and asserts it does NOT compose with the provider.
//
// The `oaep-probe` world proves the same for the decryption mints; each
// probe imports nothing the provider withholds except its own interface,
// so each failure can only come from that interface — the provider's
// kind-only `public-encryption` export rebinds the key resources and
// orphans the import (the mechanism is documented on
// `../oaep-probe/wit/world.wit` and in the `class-d` recipe).
//
// The `lann:webcrypto` package lives once at the repository root `wit/`,
// pulled in through the `deps/lann-webcrypto` symlink.
package conformance:class-d-oaep-encrypt-probe;

world oaep-encrypt-probe {
    import lann:webcrypto/rsa-oaep-encrypt@0.1.0;
}
